#
# Conformance case: quality/measurement-frame-missing
# AC: YAMATO quality constraint — MeasurementFrameMissing.
#
# ex:M bears a unit (logic:unit) but no reference frame (logic:referenceFrame).
# A value expressed in a unit must declare the frame it is read in (Principle 11),
# so the violation rule must derive violation(M, MeasurementFrameMissing). The
# foundation chase is all-IRI, so the rule keys on the IRI-valued logic:unit
# witness, not the literal logic:measuredValue. The chase seeds only from
# input.nq world facts; this program is the mirror axiom.

@prefix logic: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/> .
@prefix ex:    <https://example.org/quality/measurement-frame-missing/> .

ex:M logic:unit ex:mmHg .
